      "description": "Digested slurry is diluted and dosed with flocculant in the feedwell; flocs settle quickly, leaving clear pregnant liquor that overflows to security (polishing) filtration. The mud compacts in the lower zone and the rakes move it to the underflow cone. Overflow clarity (often ≲ 100 mg/L solids) and underflow density are the key performance targets.",
